WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:03.030
"The Batman" is back and better than ever.

00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:08.090
At 2019's DC FanDome event, the first teaser
of "The Batman" was released to the world,

00:00:08.090 --> 00:00:12.790
and it promised to be a spectacle from the
get-go. Now that some lucky audiences have

00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:17.570
been able to check out the movie, it's confirmed
that this film is everything it was suspected

00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:23.010
of being — a riveting dark thriller with
one of the best Batmans ever to don the cowl.

00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:27.419
Even before fans were able to get themselves
in seats, critics and press members were able

00:00:27.419 --> 00:00:31.579
to see Matt Reeves' take on the Dark Knight,
and they too — for the most part — were

00:00:31.579 --> 00:00:37.039
beyond impressed. Some of the first reactions
to "The Batman" called it "sensational," "gripping,"

00:00:37.039 --> 00:00:42.140
and "one helluva movie." When it comes to
our newest Caped Crusader, it was also said

00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:45.579
that Robert Pattinson might just be your new
favorite Batman.

00:00:45.579 --> 00:00:50.280
Of course, critics and audiences don't always
align — unless we're talking about Christopher

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:54.190
Nolan's "The Dark Knight" — so let's see
what the fans had to say on Twitter about

00:00:54.190 --> 00:00:58.260
"The Batman" and if it lives up to all the
hype.

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:02.969
"What is the price for your blind eye?"

00:01:02.969 --> 00:01:06.800
As to be expected, the biggest thing fans
are talking about on Twitter is Robert Pattinson's

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:11.510
portrayal of Batman and Bruce Wayne — which
are two very different things, by the way.

00:01:11.510 --> 00:01:16.500
It's hard to find a criticism of Battinson
on the bird app, with many praising his performance

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:18.230
as the Dark Knight.

00:01:18.230 --> 00:01:20.210
One User kept it simple, writing,

00:01:20.210 --> 00:01:23.580
"I admit I'm in love with Robert Pattinson's
Batman"

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:25.290
Meanwhile, another excitedly exclaimed,

00:01:25.290 --> 00:01:30.700
"Just saw #TheBatman and honestly Robert Pattinson
was born to play this role. DAMN!"

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:35.810
Moviegoers are ecstatic over Pattinson's ability
to capture the essence of the eponymous character

00:01:35.810 --> 00:01:38.390
as well as his billionaire counterpart.

00:01:38.390 --> 00:01:40.730
One fan made a definitive statement, tweeting,

00:01:40.730 --> 00:01:45.170
"Yeah... Robert Pattinson is the best Bruce
Wayne/Batman combo"

00:01:45.170 --> 00:01:49.530
The rest of the cast is being said to have
delivered incredible performances as well.

00:01:49.530 --> 00:01:52.620
One fan could barely keep their excitement
contained, writing,

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:57.640
"Pattinson f—ing killed it. Paul Dano as
Riddler was straight out of a horror movie.

00:01:57.640 --> 00:02:02.910
Colin [Farrell], John Turturro, Zoe Kravitz,
and Jeffrey Wright were all phenomenal. Matt

00:02:02.910 --> 00:02:06.070
Reeves made a f—ing masterpiece of a movie.
Holy s—."

00:02:06.070 --> 00:02:08.140
"Whoa! Take it easy, sweetheart."

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:12.590
While "The Batman" may be a standalone movie,
there was no way this new adventure wasn't

00:02:12.590 --> 00:02:17.030
going to be compared to "The Dark Knight,"
which many long hailed as the best superhero

00:02:17.030 --> 00:02:18.490
movie of all time.

00:02:18.490 --> 00:02:22.451
Fans who were able to catch the new film early
started comparing it to the Christopher Nolan

00:02:22.451 --> 00:02:24.350
film right away.

00:02:24.350 --> 00:02:25.520
One fan commented,

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:30.800
"#TheBatman is the second best superhero movie
of all time, just behind The Dark Knight"

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:32.720
Another fan lapped on more praise, saying

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:37.100
"@mattreevesLA gave me #TheBatman film of
my dreams. Something I've been waiting for

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:42.000
since Batman: The Animated Series. I've never
seen something &amp; have been absolutely sure

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:47.240
if something but I'm 100% sure this is the
best Batman film we've ever gotten. &amp; my absolute

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:48.400
favorite ever."

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:52.850
Overall, it seems like "The Batman" has cemented
itself as one of the greatest comic book movies

00:02:52.850 --> 00:02:57.880
of all time. While it technically is a superhero
movie, it doesn't necessarily feel like one.

00:02:57.880 --> 00:03:02.780
"The Batman" is an action-thriller to its
core, and fans couldn't be happier with it.

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:03.880
Some of the comments included -

00:03:03.880 --> 00:03:07.750
"10/10 This is the live-action Batman film
I've always wanted."

00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:10.820
"#TheBatman WAS SO AMAZING IM SHAKING."

00:03:10.820 --> 00:03:14.380
"Just walked out of #TheBatman and I have
no words"

00:03:14.380 --> 00:03:16.970
"They nailed #TheBatman from start to finish."

00:03:16.970 --> 00:03:21.400
"#TheBatman is a masterpiece. One of the best
superhero movies ever."

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:25.560
All in all, fans of the Dark Knight are not
going to be disappointed with "The Batman,"

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:28.320
which sounds from all reactions like it's
been worth the years of hype.

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:39.209
"When that light hits the sky, it's not just
a call – it's a warning."

